              <h2>The 6 Best Alternatives to Pok Pok</h2>

              <!-- 1. KIDAMAME DISCOVERY -->
              <div class="app-review-card kidamame-pick">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill"><i class="fa-solid fa-seedling"></i> Best Subscription-Free Montessori
                      Pick (Ages 4–10)</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">1. Kidamame Discovery</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 4–10</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-infinity"></i> One-Time Purchase (No Subscription)</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-spa"></i> Low-Stimulation</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-plane-departure"></i> 100% Offline</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  We created <strong><a href="/discovery/">Kidamame Discovery</a></strong> with the exact same core
                  conviction that makes Pok Pok so special: children deserve digital spaces that are peaceful,
                  unhurried, and free of manipulative game mechanics. Where Kidamame Discovery differs, and why it makes
                  the ideal next step or companion, is in its <strong>focus on real-world nature</strong> and its
                  <strong>one-time ownership model</strong>.
                </p>
                <p>
                  In Montessori education for ages 4–10 (often called <em>Cosmic Education</em>), children are naturally
                  drawn to understanding the real living world: biomes, animals, plants, and geological wonders. In
                  Kidamame Discovery, kids pan across <strong>6 richly illustrated ecosystems</strong>: the Alps, African
                  Savannah, Australian Outback, Arctic, Sonoran Desert, and Amazon Rainforest.
                </p>
                <ul>
                  <li><strong>Pure Child-Led Exploration:</strong> There are no scores, timers, or puzzles to fail. Kids
                    tap over 120 animals, plants, and natural phenomena (from erupting volcanoes to calving glaciers) to
                    hear authentic nature sounds and watch gentle animations.</li>
                  <li><strong>~400 Fascinating Science Facts:</strong> Tapping the magnifying glass opens illustrated
                    "Did You Know?" cards designed for co-reading with a parent or independent reading for older kids.
                  </li>
                  <li><strong>No Recurring Fees Ever:</strong> Try the app for free. If your family loves it, a single
                    one-time purchase unlocks everything forever, with zero ads, zero tracking, and 100% offline play.
                  </li>
                </ul>
                <%- include('../../partials/guide-kidamame-gallery') %>
              </div>

              <!-- 2. TINYBOP -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best Interactive Science Dioramas</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">2. Tinybop's Explorer's Library (The Earth, Mammals,
                      Plants)</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 4–10</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> Individual App Purchases</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-flask"></i> STEM &amp; Science</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Like Pok Pok, <a href="https://tinybop.com/apps" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tinybop</a>
                  emphasizes open-ended sandbox curiosity without rules or time limits. Their <em>Explorer's
                    Library</em> series includes standalone apps like <em>The Human Body</em>, <em>Mammals</em>,
                  <em>Plants</em>, and <em>The Earth</em>, where children can peer inside a kangaroo's pouch, trigger
                  earthquakes, or see how a heart beats.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why parents love it:</strong> Each Tinybop app is illustrated by a different guest artist and
                  features subtle, atmospheric sound design. Many of their individual titles can be purchased outright
                  on the App Store without a subscription, and they come with free downloadable parent handbooks to help
                  answer your child's biggest science questions.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- 3. BUSY SHAPES -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best Montessori Logic App for Toddlers (2–5)</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">3. Busy Shapes (by Edoki Academy)</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 2–6</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> Standalone Purchase Available</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-shapes"></i> Montessori Reasoning</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Inspired by the pioneering developmental work of Jean Piaget and Maria Montessori, <a
                    href="https://www.edokiacademy.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Busy Shapes</a> gives
                  young children a calm workspace to experiment with shapes, colors, and hidden obstacles. There is no
                  text, no voiceover nagging, and no countdown clock, making it very close in spirit to Pok Pok's spatial
                  toys.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why parents love it:</strong> The app uses an intelligent adaptive engine that gently
                  introduces new physical mechanics (such as sliding walls, puddles, or moving platforms) only when your
                  child is ready, fostering deep concentration and independent problem-solving.
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- 4. THINKROLLS -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best Calm Physics &amp; Problem-Solving</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">4. Thinkrolls &amp; Thinkrolls: Kings &amp; Queens (by
                      Avokiddo)</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 3–8</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> One-Time Purchase (Classic Titles)</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-gears"></i> Logic &amp; Physics</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  While family-run studio <a href="https://avokiddo.com/" target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer">Avokiddo</a> also offers a subscription bundle (<em>Thinkrolls Play &amp;
                    Code</em>), their award-winning standalone <em>Thinkrolls</em>, <em>Thinkrolls 2</em>, and
                  <em>Thinkrolls: Kings &amp; Queens</em> apps remain available as classic one-time purchases.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why parents love it:</strong> Kids guide charming rolling characters through calm, thoughtful
                  physics mazes using gears, bridges, elasticity, and gravity at their own pace. There are no time
                  limits and no lives to lose, so children learn trial-and-error reasoning without frustration.
                </p>
              </div>

