                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best Gentle Pretend Play for Ages 2–5</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">5. Sago Mini (Standalone Classics)</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 2–5</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-face-smile"></i> Gentle Humor &amp; Storytelling</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Before launching its subscription bundle, Canadian studio <a href="https://sagomini.com/"
                    target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sago Mini</a> built its reputation on sweet, slow-paced
                  pretend-play apps like <em>Sago Mini Forest Flyer</em>, <em>Ocean Swimmer</em>, and <em>Friends</em>.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why parents love it:</strong> For toddlers who love Pok Pok's open-ended discovery, Sago
                  Mini's lovable animal characters (Harvey the Dog, Jinja the Cat, and Robin the Bird) offer a warm,
                  rule-free world filled with gentle visual humor and intuitive single-tap controls. (You can also read
                  our <a href="/guides/sago-mini-alternatives/">Sago Mini Alternatives guide</a> for older kids.)
                </p>
              </div>

              <!-- 6. SEEK BY INATURALIST -->
              <div class="app-review-card">
                <div class="app-review-header">
                  <div>
                    <span class="app-pick-pill neutral">Best Free App for Real-World Outdoor Discovery</span>
                    <h3 style="margin-top: 0.6rem !important;">6. Seek by iNaturalist</h3>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="app-specs-bar">
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-child"></i> Ages 5–12+ (with Parent)</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-tag"></i> 100% Free &amp; Privacy-Safe</span>
                  <span><i class="fa-solid fa-camera"></i> Outdoor Nature ID</span>
                </div>
                <p>
                  Montessori philosophy always points children back toward the real outdoors. Created by the California
                  Academy of Sciences and National Geographic, <a href="https://www.inaturalist.org/pages/seek_app"
                    target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Seek by iNaturalist</a> requires no registration, collects
                  no user data, and lets kids point a phone or tablet camera at leaves, flowers, mushrooms, and insects
                  in your backyard or local park to identify them in real time.
                </p>
                <p>
                  <strong>Why parents love it:</strong> It is 100% free, non-profit, and turns every family walk into a
                  hands-on biology lesson. Pair it with <strong>Kidamame Discovery</strong> on rainy days or flights for
                  a complete indoor-and-outdoor nature toolkit!
                </p>
              </div>

